{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Better is open reproof:</b> The word תוכחת stands in place of two, i.e., open reproof — that they reprove him openly — is better than hidden reproof of love, i.e., that his loved ones reprove him in secret. Better than it is the open one, for in the open he will be ashamed and chastised."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:59.549057637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}